// Secrets.example.xcconfig — template. Copy to Secrets.xcconfig (gitignored):
//
//     cp studytimer/Config/Secrets.example.xcconfig studytimer/Config/Secrets.xcconfig
//
// Base.xcconfig pulls it in with #include?, so a missing file is not a build
// error — the app just runs fully offline and shows "medx sync: not configured".
//
// This is not really a secret. The backend authenticates every request against
// one shared password that is hardcoded in the repo (api/studytime.js), and it
// treats a *missing* password as valid — `if (pass && pass !== PASSWORD)` — so
// the endpoint is effectively open. It's kept out of tracked source out of
// hygiene rather than because it protects anything. If that endpoint ever gets
// real auth, move this to the keychain the way ios/Shared/Net/AppSecrets.swift
// does.

MEDX_PASSWORD =
